[Music]  a district court judge denied an effort  by president trump's campaign and the  nevada republican party  to delay the county of mail ballots in  clark county  thank you for joining us on 8 news now  at 6 30 i'm brian loftis  and i'm denise valdez so in that lawsuit  which was filed back in late october  attorneys for the trump campaign claimed  it was impossible to accurately check  signatures  and verify every ballot clark county  elections chief joe gloria testified  that not using the signature scanner  would just require a massive overhaul  the trump campaign also alleged they  were not able to record while they were  observing ballot counting  clark county argued that observers are  allowed but recording  violates nevada law the request to stop  mail ballot county was denied by a  carson city judge  this morning talked with nevada trump  campaign co-chair and former attorney  general adam laxalt  who is leading the charge on these  lawsuits and he says he is fighting for  transparency for all voters you have  nearly 500 thousand mail-in ballots  coming through the clark county system  a machine is approving 30 to 40 percent  of those  and if it's approved it counts so no  human being touches those  and then it goes to workers  and it's a hallmark of our system  now a third lawsuit filed by the trump  campaign had a hearing today and that  lawsuit seeks to get information about  signature checkers such as their  political official their political  affiliations clark county says the  election panels are all bipartisan  though  laxalt says if necessary they are  prepared to take that fight to the  supreme court  a spokesperson for the clark county said  in a statement the county was pleased  with the decision to halt the second  lawsuit  they released a statement that said in  part we fully agree with the judge and  appreciate his clear rulings on the  matters raised  this is the busiest time of the year for  the election department  and we are glad to have another baseless  lawsuit dismissed so quickly  nevada attorney general aaron ford also  releasing a statement saying in part  today's ruling makes clear that there is  proper procedure to observe an election  that even the president must follow and  it's most certainly a victory for the  constitutional rights of all nevadans

